// Every `as` the spec allows between f16 -> bf16, bf16 -> f16, compiled, linked and run:
// 1 as T as S is 1 again (true for bool), for every ordered pair whose
// class is not X (conversion-lattice.mdx s1: I, W and E all take `as`).
// 1 is exact in every type here, so a miss is a wrong conversion, and a
// C++ error is a cast EmitIR spelled that clang refuses. A failing pair
// prints its names; the exit code counts them. Each value comes out of
// a call (one_S), so the casts are runtime conversions at -O0.
//
// XFAIL: *
// Ticket "[Codegen] `f16 as bf16` / `bf16 as f16` emit a static_cast clang
// refuses" (2026-10-28). Both are E (R4: every float pair but the three
// widenings), so Sema accepts them, and EmitIR's _cast spells every numeric
// `as` as static_cast<T>(x). clang has no direct _Float16 <-> __bf16
// conversion: CL001E "static_cast from '_Float16' to '__bf16' is not
